rmvol: Moving file metadata
    file name: /var/adm/ris/ris0.alpha/product_2/DPORTL560
rmvol: Moving file metadata
    file name: /var/adm/ris/ris0.alpha/product_2/instctrl/DPOBASE560.scp
[...]

and so on repeating the same block of text all the time. 

showfdmn tells us the following:

               Id              Date Created  LogPgs  Version  Domain Name
408a4ca2.00098611  Sat Apr 24 13:16:50 2004     512        4  ext_misc

  Vol   512-Blks        Free  % Used  Cmode  Rblks  Wblks  Vol Name
   1L    5924496     5909136      0%     on    256    256  /dev/disk/dsk4a
   2     5924496     4222432     29%     on    256    256  /dev/disk/dsk4b
   3     5924496     3635904     39%     on    256    256  /dev/disk/dsk4d
      ----------  ----------  ------
        17773488    13767472     23%

We tried to remove /dev/disk/dsk4a. You may notice that the domain consists
of partitions of only one physical volume. This was for testing purposes but
we encountered the described problem in the same way when doing rmvol on
domains consisting of several drives.

We did an extensive web search hoping someone else had encountered (and
solved) this problem before but couldn't find anything useful.

Finally, you may be interested in our configuration. We did the rmvol on a
digital Personal Workstation 500au with Tru64 Unix V 5.1B and uname -a says

OSF1 XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX V5.1 2650 alpha

The machine has 640 MB Ram and a qlogic SCSI controller. The harddiscs are
connected through external UltraWide SCSI and are arranged in a StorageWorks
block.

If you have a tip for us, we would be glad to hear from you.

