Hello!

I have a new installed v5.1 on an AS 500/400 and an AS 600. If I try to get 
data from a nfs-import from a XP1000 working with v5.0 i get on the client:

May 18 22:47:18 omega vmunix: NFS3 server delta not responding still trying
May 18 22:47:21 omega vmunix: NFS3 server alpha not responding still trying
May 18 22:47:25 omega vmunix: NFS3 server delta not responding still trying
May 18 22:47:37 omega vmunix: NFS3 server delta ok
May 18 22:47:38 omega vmunix: NFS3 server delta not responding still trying
and so on...

and on the server:
May 18 22:47:23 delta vmunix: svckudp_send: xdr_replymsg failed
May 18 22:47:23 delta vmunix: rfs_dispatch: sendreply failed IP address: 
129.217.226.24
and so on...

Accessing data greater than a few kb fails.

The same things happen with a nfs-import from an ES40 also working with 
v5.0. But all is fine with a nfs-import from a XP1000 working with v4.0E. 
Also network-communication with SUN-Workstations seems to be all right.

NFS works between the 2 XP1000 an the ES40 without errors in all directions.
Pings from any of the workstations to any other results without any loss.

For this reasons i think it is a problem between the nfs-server in v5.0 and 
the nfs-client in v5.1, but I was unable to find a solution on the web.

Any suggestions?

